From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alan Shearer <sakison@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 13:40:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] power_daemon: set scheduler mode from AC state

Read /boot/system/settings/power_daemon. If power saving on battery
is on, switch to power saving when AC is offline. Switch back to
low latency when AC is online, unless keep power saving on AC is set.

Apply that at startup, on an AC read, and when the preferences app
sends 'PwRl'. No AC device means leave the mode alone. The option
stays off until the settings file says otherwise.

---
 src/servers/power/Jamfile            |  1 +
 src/servers/power/ac_monitor.cpp     | 23 +++++++++++++++++----
 src/servers/power/ac_monitor.h       |  2 ++
 src/servers/power/power_daemon.cpp   | 32 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 src/servers/power/power_settings.cpp | 49 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/servers/power/power_settings.h   | 20 ++++++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 121 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/servers/power/power_settings.cpp
 create mode 100644 src/servers/power/power_settings.h

diff --git a/src/servers/power/Jamfile b/src/servers/power/Jamfile
